From 419fd68eac8fe21bcbdf6b6b301d05985894be00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:57:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HCG Jailbreak Academy: publish academy/ behind [academy]
 enabled (off by default)

- config/repo.toml: new [academy] section, enabled = false. A Publish run cannot release the guide until the owner
  turns it on; a non-boolean value is a configuration error.
- site.copy_academy: copies academy/ (html, css, js, images; not data/ or README) to <site>/academy/ and fails the
  build if required files are missing. Stable channel only.
- page(): optional Academy link in the primary navigation, shown only when enabled.
- site.css: on screens up to 520 px the navigation wraps onto its own row. Fixes an existing overflow at 320 px, where
  'Help' was cut off by body overflow-x: hidden, which a fourth link would have made worse.
- tests/test_academy.py: disabled build has no academy and no link; enabled build publishes it, links it from every
  page, resolves every local reference and still verifies; missing files fail; non-boolean config fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QS5EmhpxQHv4LAEhMadUA6
