+<!-- ======================================================================= 1 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-1" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-1-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Basics</p><h2 id="ch-1-h">What is jailbreaking?</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p>An iPhone only runs software that Apple has approved and signed, and every app is kept inside its own <strong>sandbox</strong>, a fenced-off area it cannot leave. Those rules are a large part of why iOS is secure.</p>
+    <p><strong>Jailbreaking</strong> uses security flaws in iOS (<strong>exploits</strong>) to lift some of those rules on your own device. Once jailbroken, you can install software Apple would not allow, change how iOS looks and behaves, and get deeper access to the file system. ios.cfw.guide sums up what you get: “Gain full access to your device's OS”, a package manager such as Sileo or Zebra, themes, and tweaks that “change how iOS behaves”.</p>
+    <h3>How a modern jailbreak runs</h3>
+    <p>Dopamine is <strong>semi-untethered</strong>: it “requires an app to re-apply the exploit after a reboot”. The jailbreak does not survive a full restart. After every restart your device is back to normal iOS until you open the Dopamine app and tap <em>Jailbreak</em> again. A <strong>respring</strong> (restarting only the Home Screen) or a <strong>userspace reboot</strong> keeps you jailbroken.</p>
+    <figure class="fig">
+      <img src="../assets/img/diagram-cycle.svg" width="760" height="300" alt="Diagram. Stock iOS becomes jailbroken when you open Dopamine and tap Jailbreak. A respring or userspace reboot keeps the jailbreak. A full reboot, power off or a flat battery returns the device to stock iOS until you run Dopamine again.">
+      <figcaption>The semi-untethered cycle. Original HCG diagram.</figcaption>
+    </figure>
+    <h3>Is it legal?</h3>
+    <p>ios.cfw.guide notes that in the United States the Copyright Office has granted an exemption for jailbreaking since 2010, and advises you to “check in your country whether it is legal there”. Legal is not the same as supported: Apple says unauthorized modification “is a violation of the iOS and iPadOS Software License Agreement” and that it “may deny service” for a device running unauthorized software (Apple's statement as published on the official Dopamine website). <a href="#ch-4">Chapter 4</a> covers what that means in practice.</p>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/types-of-jailbreak/" rel="noopener">ios.cfw.guide: Types of Jailbreak</a>, <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/faq/" rel="noopener">FAQ</a>, <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a>.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-2">Next: Why do people jailbreak? →</a></p></div>
+</section>
+
+<!-- ======================================================================= 2 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-2" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-2-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Motivation</p><h2 id="ch-2-h">Why do people jailbreak?</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <ul>
+      <li><strong>Personalisation.</strong> Themes, Home Screen and Lock Screen layouts, animations and system behaviour that iOS settings do not offer.</li>
+      <li><strong>Features Apple does not provide.</strong> Tweaks add controls, shortcuts, gestures and options to existing apps and to iOS itself.</li>
+      <li><strong>Learning and development.</strong> A terminal, the file system and developer tools on the device are useful for students, developers and security researchers studying their own hardware.</li>
+      <li><strong>Ownership.</strong> Some people simply want full control over a device they paid for.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <div class="callout callout-info"><span class="callout-title">Do you actually need it?</span>
+      <p>If you only want a feature Shortcuts, Focus modes, widgets or an App Store app can provide, use those: they keep every iOS protection. Jailbreak because you understand the trade-offs in Chapters 3 and 4, not because a video made it look easy.</p></div>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-1">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-3">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
+
+<!-- ======================================================================= 3 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-3" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-3-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Trade-offs</p><h2 id="ch-3-h">Benefits and limitations</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <div class="compare">
+      <div class="card"><h3>Benefits</h3><ul class="pros">
+        <li>Tweaks, themes and command-line tools from package managers.</li>
+        <li>Deeper file-system access (within the rootless limits of <a href="#ch-5">Chapter 5</a>).</li>
+        <li>Dopamine is open source and removable from its own app.</li>
+        <li>Semi-untethered: a normal restart always gives you stock iOS back, which makes many problems easy to escape.</li>
+      </ul></div>
+      <div class="card"><h3>Limitations</h3><ul class="cons">
+        <li><strong>You are frozen on old iOS.</strong> Dopamine supports specific versions only; updating usually ends your ability to jailbreak.</li>
+        <li>You must re-run Dopamine after every full restart.</li>
+        <li>On the sideloading route the Dopamine app must be re-signed every 7 days.</li>
+        <li>Tweaks must be built for rootless jailbreaks and for your iOS version; many older tweaks are not.</li>
+        <li>Banking, payment, some games and other apps may refuse to run.</li>
+        <li>Tweaks can make the device unstable and drain the battery.</li>
+      </ul></div>
+    </div>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/installing-dopamine/" rel="noopener">ios.cfw.guide: Installing Dopamine</a>, <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a>, <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/blocking-jailbreak-detection/" rel="noopener">Blocking Jailbreak Detection</a>.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-2">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-4">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
+
+<!-- ======================================================================= 4 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-4" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-4-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Read before you decide</p><h2 id="ch-4-h">Security, privacy, stability and warranty risks</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p>The official Dopamine website opens with Apple's warning, quoted here because it is the fairest summary of the downside:</p>
+    <blockquote class="callout callout-warn"><p>“Jailbreaking your device eliminates security layers designed to protect your personal information and your iOS device. With this security removed from your iPhone, hackers may steal your personal information, damage your device, attack your network, or introduce malware, spyware, or viruses.”</p>
+    <p class="source-note">Apple, as published on <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a>.</p></blockquote>
+    <h3>Security</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li><strong>Weakened protections.</strong> The jailbreak works by bypassing kernel protections (Dopamine's log shows steps such as “Exploiting Kernel”, “Bypassing PAC” and “Bypassing PPL”). Code that iOS would block can now run with elevated privileges.</li>
+      <li><strong>Old, unpatched iOS.</strong> To stay jailbreakable you stay on a version with publicly known vulnerabilities. Every security fix Apple ships later is one you do not get. This is the biggest long-term cost.</li>
+      <li><strong>Update blocking has a price.</strong> ios.cfw.guide documents a profile that stops iOS updates so you are not updated by accident. Installing it also stops security updates, and it is a configuration profile from a third party. Only install it if you accept both; remove it when you stop jailbreaking.</li>
+      <li><strong>Accounts on the device.</strong> Dopamine lets you set the password of the <code>mobile</code> user, which “can also be used for root access using sudo”. If you enable SSH or a developer shell, set a strong password first.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <h3>Privacy</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>A tweak can be loaded into almost any process, including Messages, Mail and your password manager. Install only what you trust, from sources you trust (<a href="#ch-12">Chapter 12</a>).</li>
+      <li>Malicious or pirated packages are a classic way to spread spyware on jailbroken devices.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <h3>Stability and data</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Apple lists “frequent and unexpected crashes”, “shortened battery life”, “unreliable voice and data” and disrupted services such as iCloud, iMessage, FaceTime and Apple Pay.</li>
+      <li>An incompatible tweak can cause a <strong>respring loop</strong>. ios.cfw.guide warns jailbreaking “can lead to data loss if you damage the OS”.</li>
+      <li>If your phone has a replacement screen, ios.cfw.guide warns its touchscreen may stop working after the jailbreak's userspace reboot.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <h3>Banking and other apps</h3>
+    <p>Many apps detect jailbreaks and refuse to run, including banking apps and some online games. ios.cfw.guide's own advice: “We do not recommend using banking apps on a jailbroken device. Use a separate secure device to access your bank account.” Dopamine's <em>Hide Jailbreak</em> option only removes jailbreak files temporarily and, in Dopamine's words, “is not entirely effective and does not conceal everything”. This guide does not cover defeating app security checks.</p>
+    <h3>Warranty and service</h3>
+    <p>Apple “may deny service for an iPhone that has any unauthorized software installed”. ios.cfw.guide adds that your warranty is void “until it is restored to an un-jailbroken state, which is easy to do”. Remove the jailbreak (<a href="#ch-14">Chapter 14</a>) before any repair or service appointment.</p>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a>; <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/faq/" rel="noopener">ios.cfw.guide FAQ</a>; <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/blocking-updates/" rel="noopener">Blocking Updates</a>; <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/blocking-jailbreak-detection/" rel="noopener">Blocking Jailbreak Detection</a>; Dopamine 3.0.13 app strings (<a href="https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine" rel="noopener">source</a>).</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-3">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-5">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
+
+<!-- ======================================================================= 5 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-5" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-5-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Concepts</p><h2 id="ch-5-h">Rootless versus rootful jailbreaking</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p>Older jailbreaks were <strong>rootful</strong>: they wrote their files into the system part of the disk, the root (<code>/</code>). Dopamine is <strong>rootless</strong>. In the words of its website, rootless jailbreaks “do not provide full access to the iOS device's operating system, as only certain parts of the filesystem can be written to.”</p>
+    <figure class="fig">
+      <img src="../assets/img/diagram-rootless.svg" width="760" height="330" alt="Diagram comparing the two layouts. Rootful: jailbreak files are written into the system volume at /, packages use architecture iphoneos-arm. Rootless, used by Dopamine: the system volume is left untouched and everything goes under /var/jb on the data volume, a link to a hidden folder in /private/preboot; packages use architecture iphoneos-arm64.">
+      <figcaption>Where jailbreak files live. Original HCG diagram, simplified.</figcaption>
+    </figure>
+    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Package layouts (scrollable)"><table>
+      <caption>Package layouts</caption>
+      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Layout</th><th scope="col">Package architecture</th><th scope="col">Files installed under</th><th scope="col">Examples</th></tr></thead>
+      <tbody>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Rootless</th><td><code>iphoneos-arm64</code></td><td><code>/var/jb/…</code> only</td><td>Dopamine, palera1n (rootless)</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Rootful</th><td><code>iphoneos-arm</code></td><td><code>/</code></td><td>palera1n (rootful), older jailbreaks</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Roothide</th><td><code>iphoneos-arm64e</code></td><td>a randomised jailbreak root</td><td>separate tools (not covered here)</td></tr>
+      </tbody>
+    </table></div>
+    <h3>What it means for you</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Install only tweaks built for rootless. Dopamine's website: “Users should check if their tweaks are compatible with iOS 15+ [and] are properly compiled for rootless before installing them.”</li>
+      <li>Sileo only lists packages whose architecture matches your device, so most incompatible rootful packages are simply hidden.</li>
+      <li>Developers: rebuild for rootless (Theos <code>THEOS_PACKAGE_SCHEME = rootless</code>) and resolve paths at run time with <a href="https://github.com/opa334/libroot" rel="noopener">libroot</a> rather than hard-coding <code>/var/jb</code>.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a>; HCG Repo <a href="https://github.com/F1r3srp3nt/HCG-repo/blob/main/docs/ROOTLESS_ROOTFUL.md" rel="noopener">docs/ROOTLESS_ROOTFUL.md</a> (Theos rootless guide, Procursus, Sileo source review).</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-4">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-6">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
+
+<!-- ======================================================================= 6 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-6" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-6-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div><p class="eyebrow">The example</p><h2 id="ch-6-h">What is Dopamine?</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p><strong>Dopamine</strong> is “a rootless semi-untethered jailbreak” for iPhone and iPad (its README). It is open source under the MIT License, led by Lars Fröder (opa334) with a team its website credits as main developers: kok3shidoll, Alfie, TheRealClarity, staturnz and wh1te4ever. HCG is not part of that team.</p>
+    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Dopamine at a glance (reviewed 21 Nov 2026) (scrollable)"><table>
+      <caption>Dopamine at a glance (reviewed 21 Nov 2026)</caption>
+      <tbody>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Latest release</th><td>3.0.13 (tagged 3 November 2026)</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Type</th><td>Rootless, semi-untethered</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Chips</th><td>arm64: A8 – A11 · arm64e: A12 – A17, M1 – M2</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Versions</th><td>iOS/iPadOS 15.0 – 17.3.1 on all supported chips; 17.4 – 18.7.1 and 26.0 – 26.0.1 on A13 and earlier (<a href="#ch-7">details</a>)</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Package managers offered</th><td>Sileo, Zebra</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Tweak injection</th><td>ElleKit, by évelyne</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Official download</th><td><a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a> and <a href="https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine/releases/latest" rel="noopener">GitHub releases</a></td></tr>
+      </tbody>
+    </table></div>
+    <h3>What is inside the app</h3>
+    <p>The app has a <em>Jailbreak</em> button and a menu with <em>Settings</em>, <em>Restart SpringBoard</em>, <em>Reboot Userspace</em> and <em>Credits</em>. In <em>Settings</em>:</p>
+    <ul>
+      <li><strong>Tweak Injection</strong>: loads your tweaks. Turning it off is how you start without tweaks (Safe Mode, <a href="#ch-13">Chapter 13</a>). Changing it needs a userspace reboot.</li>
+      <li><strong>Verbose Logs</strong>, <strong>Allow JIT in Apps</strong>, <strong>Allow Legacy arm64e Libraries</strong>, <strong>Jetsam Multiplier</strong> and <strong>iDownload (Developer Shell)</strong>: advanced options. Leave them alone unless a guide you trust tells you otherwise.</li>
+      <li><strong>Exploits</strong>: which kernel exploit and bypasses to use. The app marks its choice as <em>Recommended</em>; keep it.</li>
+      <li><strong>Refresh Jailbreak Apps</strong>, <strong>Reinstall Package Managers</strong>, <strong>Change “mobile” Password</strong>, <strong>Hide Jailbreak</strong> and <strong>Remove Jailbreak</strong>.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <div class="phones">
+      <figure><img src="../assets/img/dp-main.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration of Dopamine's main screen: the Dopamine logo, Settings and Credits rows, and a large Jailbreak button."><figcaption>Main screen (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+      <figure><img src="../assets/img/dp-settings.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration of Dopamine Settings: Tweak Injection switched on, Verbose Logs off, and actions Refresh Jailbreak Apps, Reinstall Package Managers, Change mobile Password, Hide Jailbreak and Remove Jailbreak."><figcaption>Settings (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+    </div>
+    <p class="small muted">Illustrations are original drawings using the wording of Dopamine 3.0.13's English interface. Layout and colours differ from the real app.</p>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine" rel="noopener">Dopamine README, LICENSE.md and app strings (3.0.13)</a>; <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a> (credits, chips, package managers).</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-5">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-7">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
