+<section class="chapter" id="ch-7" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-7-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Interactive</p><h2 id="ch-7-h">Device and firmware compatibility</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p>Not every iOS version can be jailbroken, and the newest never can. Dopamine's published support, word for word from its sources:</p>
+    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Dopamine 3.0.13 supported ranges (scrollable)"><table>
+      <caption>Dopamine 3.0.13 supported ranges</caption>
+      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Chips</th><th scope="col">iOS / iPadOS</th><th scope="col">Source wording</th></tr></thead>
+      <tbody>
+        <tr><td>A8 – A17, M1 – M2 (all supported)</td><td>15.0 – 17.3.1</td><td>“Supported on iOS 15.0 - 17.3.1 (A14 - A17 / M1 - M2)” and below</td></tr>
+        <tr><td>A8 – A13 (A13 and earlier)</td><td>17.4 – 18.7.1</td><td>“iOS 15.0 - 18.7.1 (arm64)” · “iOS 15.0 - 18.7.1, 26.0 - 26.0.1 (A12/A13)”</td></tr>
+        <tr><td>A12 – A13 in practice (older chips never received iOS 26)</td><td>26.0 – 26.0.1</td><td>“Supported on iOS 15.0 - 18.7.1 and 26.0 - 26.0.1 (A8 - A13)”</td></tr>
+      </tbody>
+    </table></div>
+    <p>Everything else is <strong>not supported</strong>, including 18.7.2 and later, 26.1 and later, 27.x, and every device with an A18, A19, A20, M3, M4 or M5 chip.</p>
+    <figure class="fig">
+      <img src="../assets/img/diagram-route.svg" width="760" height="360" alt="Table diagram of installation routes. 15.0 to 16.6.1: TrollStore route, permanent install. 16.7 RC (20H18) and 17.0: TrollStore route via TrollRestore, needs a computer. 16.7 to 16.7.x and 17.0.1 to 17.3.1: sideload route on all supported chips, re-sign every 7 days. 17.4 to 18.7.1: sideload route on A13 and earlier only. 26.0 to 26.0.1: sideload route on A13 and earlier only. Anything else: not supported.">
+      <figcaption>Which route applies to which version. Original HCG diagram based on ios.cfw.guide.</figcaption>
+    </figure>
+
+    <h3 id="checker-h">Check your device</h3>
+    <p>Find your answers in <strong>Settings › General › About</strong>: <em>Model Name</em>, <em>iOS Version</em>, and <em>Model Number</em> (tap it to switch to the number beginning with A, such as A2161). The checker runs entirely in your browser, sends nothing anywhere and never stores your answers.</p>
+    <form id="checker" class="card" aria-labelledby="checker-h" novalidate>
+      <div class="checker-grid">
+        <div>
+          <div class="field">
+            <label for="cc-filter">Search for your model</label>
+            <input class="input" id="cc-filter" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. iPhone 12, A2161, iPhone13,2" aria-describedby="cc-filter-help">
+            <p class="help" id="cc-filter-help">Name, model number (A…), identifier or chip. The list below narrows as you type.</p>
+          </div>
+          <div class="field">
+            <label for="cc-device">Exact iPhone or iPad model</label>
+            <select class="select" id="cc-device" aria-describedby="cc-facts"><option value="">Choose your model…</option></select>
+            <p class="device-facts" id="cc-facts" aria-live="polite"></p>
+          </div>
+          <div class="field">
+            <label for="cc-version">Installed iOS / iPadOS version</label>
+            <input class="input" id="cc-version" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" list="cc-versions" placeholder="e.g. 16.6.1" aria-describedby="cc-version-help">
+            <datalist id="cc-versions"></datalist>
+            <p class="help" id="cc-version-help">Exactly as shown under iOS Version. Suggestions list the versions Apple released for the model you chose.</p>
+          </div>
+          <fieldset class="field" id="cc-build-row" hidden>
+            <legend>Build number for 16.7</legend>
+            <p class="help">Shown in brackets next to the version in Settings › General › About, e.g. 16.7 (20H18).</p>
+            <div class="choices">
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-build" value="20H18"><span>20H18 (Release Candidate)</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-build" value="20H19"><span>20H19 or another</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-build" value="unsure" checked><span>Not sure</span></label>
+            </div>
+          </fieldset>
+        </div>
+        <div>
+          <fieldset class="field">
+            <legend>Is a jailbreak installed already?</legend>
+            <div class="choices">
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-jb" value="none" checked><span>No</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-jb" value="dopamine"><span>Dopamine</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-jb" value="palera1n-rootless"><span>palera1n (rootless)</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-jb" value="palera1n-rootful"><span>palera1n (rootful)</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-jb" value="other-rootless"><span>nathanlr, Relaxin, Serotonin or Bootstrap</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-jb" value="older"><span>Another jailbreak</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-jb" value="unsure"><span>Not sure</span></label>
+            </div>
+          </fieldset>
+          <fieldset class="field">
+            <legend>Is TrollStore installed?</legend>
+            <div class="choices">
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-ts" value="no" checked><span>No</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-ts" value="yes"><span>Yes</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-ts" value="unsure"><span>Not sure</span></label>
+            </div>
+          </fieldset>
+          <fieldset class="field">
+            <legend>Do you have a current backup?</legend>
+            <div class="choices">
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-backup" value="yes"><span>Yes, made today or recently</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-backup" value="no" checked><span>No</span></label>
+            </div>
+          </fieldset>
+          <fieldset class="field">
+            <legend>Has this device ever installed an iOS update?</legend>
+            <p class="help">The sideloading guide does not work on the version a device originally shipped with.</p>
+            <div class="choices">
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-fw" value="updated" checked><span>Yes</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-fw" value="factory"><span>No, never updated</span></label>
+              <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="cc-fw" value="unsure"><span>Not sure</span></label>
+            </div>
+          </fieldset>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+      <div class="form-actions">
+        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Check compatibility</button>
+        <button type="reset" class="btn btn-metal">Clear</button>
+      </div>
+      <div id="cc-result" class="verdict" aria-live="polite"></div>
+      <noscript><p class="callout callout-info">The checker needs JavaScript. Without it, compare your chip and version with the table above and the official guides.</p></noscript>
+    </form>
+    <p class="small muted">Results: <span class="badge badge-ok">Supported</span> a documented route fits and nothing else is needed first · <span class="badge badge-warn">Requirements</span> supported once you meet the listed conditions · <span class="badge badge-danger">Unsupported</span> outside Dopamine's published ranges · <span class="badge badge-info">Not verified</span> we cannot match your answers to a real model and release, or no documented route fits. The checker never guesses.</p>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine" rel="noopener">Dopamine README</a>, <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a>, <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/installing-dopamine/" rel="noopener">ios.cfw.guide</a> (routes), <a href="https://github.com/opa334/TrollStore" rel="noopener">TrollStore README</a>; device and release data from <a href="https://github.com/littlebyteorg/appledb" rel="noopener">AppleDB</a>, the database ellekit.space links to for “a more detailed breakdown”.</p>
+  </div>
