+<!-- ======================================================================= 8 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-8" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-8-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Before you start</p><h2 id="ch-8-h">Preparing your iPhone and backing up</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p>ios.cfw.guide “strongly” recommends a backup and says that “if no issues occur during installation, you will be jailbroken without any data loss”. Prepare for the case where issues do occur.</p>
+    <h3 id="checklist-h">Preparation checklist</h3>
+    <p class="checklist-status" aria-live="polite">0 of 10 preparation items done.</p>
+    <ul class="checklist" aria-labelledby="checklist-h">
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-check"><span>The checker in Chapter 7 says <em>Supported</em> or <em>Requirements</em> for my exact model and version, and I have met every listed requirement.<span class="why">Never rely on a video or a friend's phone: support depends on the exact chip and version.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-backup"><span>I made a full backup today: iCloud, or an <strong>encrypted</strong> backup in Finder or iTunes.<span class="why">Encrypted computer backups also keep saved passwords and Health data. Check that it finished.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-photos"><span>Photos and important files are also synced or copied somewhere else.<span class="why">A second copy protects you if a backup turns out to be incomplete.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-updates"><span>Automatic updates are off (Settings › General › Software Update › Automatic Updates).<span class="why">An accidental update can permanently end your ability to jailbreak.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-power"><span>The battery is well charged or the device is plugged in.<span class="why">ios.cfw.guide: prevent “any unexpected power off”.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-account"><span>I know my Apple Account password and passcode, and I can receive two-factor codes.<span class="why">Needed for sideloading, restores and Activation Lock.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-computer"><span>If my route needs a computer, it is ready with the tools from Chapter 9 (and iTunes on Windows).<span class="why">TrollRestore, TrollInstallerMDC and sideloading need one.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-oldjb"><span>No conflicting jailbreak is installed (rootful palera1n, nathanlr, Relaxin, Serotonin, Bootstrap).<span class="why">ios.cfw.guide requires removing these first.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-banking"><span>I accept that banking and some other apps may stop working, and I have another way to reach them.<span class="why">See Chapter 4.</span></span></label></li>
+      <li><label><input type="checkbox" id="prep-recovery"><span>I have read how to get out of trouble (Chapter 13) and how to remove the jailbreak (Chapter 14).<span class="why">Know the way back before you leave.</span></span></label></li>
+    </ul>
+    <h3>What a backup can and cannot do</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>A backup restores your <strong>data</strong>. It does not restore your iOS version or your jailbreak.</li>
+      <li>Restoring the phone with a computer installs a version Apple still signs, normally the newest. That usually ends jailbreak support for good, and you cannot choose to go back to an older version.</li>
+      <li>A backup made on a newer iOS version cannot be restored to a device running an older one.</li>
+      <li>Keep a backup from <em>before</em> you jailbreak. Backups made while jailbroken can carry tweak settings and leftovers back to a clean phone.</li>
+    </ul>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-7">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-9">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
