+<!-- ======================================================================= 9 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-9" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-9-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Installation</p><h2 id="ch-9-h">Installing Dopamine</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <div class="callout callout-warn" id="install-gate"><span class="callout-title">Preparation not finished</span><p>Your checklist in <a href="#checklist-h">Chapter 8</a> is not complete. You can read on, but finish it before you change anything on your device.</p></div>
+    <p>These steps summarise the official ios.cfw.guide instructions for Dopamine. Follow the official page side by side: if it differs from this summary, it wins. HCG has no way to install anything on your device.</p>
+    <h3>Get the official Dopamine package</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Download <code>Dopamine.ipa</code> only from <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a> (“Download .ipa”, or “Open in TrollStore”) or from <a href="https://github.com/opa334/Dopamine/releases/latest" rel="noopener">github.com/opa334/Dopamine/releases</a>.</li>
+      <li>Do not use copies from mirrors, “signing services”, video descriptions, Discord files or HCG: HCG does not host Dopamine. A modified jailbreak runs with full control of your phone.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>Then follow the route the checker gave you. Use the tabs below (arrow keys switch tabs).</p>
+
+    <div class="tabs">
+      <div role="tablist" aria-label="Installation route">
+        <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-trollstore" aria-controls="panel-trollstore" aria-selected="true">TrollStore route (15.0 – 16.6.1, 16.7 RC, 17.0)</button>
+        <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-sideload" aria-controls="panel-sideload" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Sideload route (16.7 – 16.7.x, 17.0.1 and later)</button>
+      </div>
+
+      <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-trollstore" aria-labelledby="tab-trollstore" tabindex="0">
+        <p class="route-note">TrollStore permanently installs Dopamine, so it never expires. TrollStore itself can only run on 14.0 beta 2 – 16.6.1, 16.7 RC (20H18) and 17.0 (TrollStore README).</p>
+        <h4>Part A. Install TrollStore (skip if you have it)</h4>
+        <p>The method depends on your chip and version. The checker names your method; the official page has a tab for each:</p>
+        <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="TrollStore installers (ios.cfw.guide) (scrollable)"><table>
+          <caption>TrollStore installers (ios.cfw.guide)</caption>
+          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Method</th><th scope="col">Versions</th><th scope="col">Computer</th></tr></thead>
+          <tbody>
+            <tr><th scope="row">TrollHelperOTA</th><td>15.0 – 15.4.1; A12 and later 15.5 – 15.6.1</td><td>Not needed</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">TrollInstallerX</th><td>16.0 – 16.6.1; A9(X) and later 15.7 – 15.8.6; A9(X) – A11 15.5 – 15.6.1</td><td>Needed unless jailbreaks.app signs it</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">TrollRestore</th><td>15.8.7 – 15.8.8; 16.7 RC (20H18); 17.0; A8(X) 15.7.2 – 15.8.6</td><td>Needed; Find My must be off during it</td></tr>
+            <tr><th scope="row">TrollInstallerMDC</th><td>A8(X) 15.5 – 15.7.1</td><td>Needed</td></tr>
+          </tbody>
+        </table></div>
+        <p>Follow your method's tab on <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/installing-dopamine-trollstore/" rel="noopener">Installing Dopamine (TrollStore)</a>, including <strong>Install Persistence Helper</strong>. TrollStore's README explains why: when iOS reloads its icon cache, TrollStore apps stop launching until the persistence helper re-registers them.</p>
+        <h4>Part B. Install Dopamine with TrollStore</h4>
+        <ol class="walk">
+          <li><strong>Save the .ipa on the device.</strong> Download <code>Dopamine.ipa</code> from the official site in Safari (or tap “Open in TrollStore” there).</li>
+          <li><strong>Open TrollStore</strong> and tap <em>+</em> at the top right.</li>
+          <li><strong>Choose the file.</strong> Go to where you saved the Dopamine <code>.ipa</code> and tap it.</li>
+          <li><strong>Tap Install.</strong> Dopamine appears on your Home Screen. No trust step and no Developer Mode are needed on this route.</li>
+        </ol>
+        <div class="phones">
+          <figure><img src="../assets/img/ts-plus.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration: TrollStore's Apps tab, with the plus button at the top right highlighted."><figcaption>Step 2 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+          <figure><img src="../assets/img/ts-file.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration: a file picker showing the Downloads folder with Dopamine.ipa highlighted."><figcaption>Step 3 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+          <figure><img src="../assets/img/ts-install.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration: TrollStore asks “Install this app?” for Dopamine, with Install highlighted."><figcaption>Step 4 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-sideload" aria-labelledby="tab-sideload" tabindex="0" hidden>
+        <p class="route-note">For 16.7 – 16.7.x (not 16.7 RC) and 17.0.1 or later, where TrollStore cannot run. The app is signed with your Apple Account and must be <strong>re-signed every 7 days</strong>. This route does not work on the iOS version a device originally shipped with.</p>
+        <div class="callout callout-info"><span class="callout-title">No computer?</span><p>ios.cfw.guide says the computer is only needed “unless jailbreaks.app is signed”. When we reviewed it, the guide said jailbreaks.app was signing <strong>Dopamine 2.5b4</strong>, an older version than 3.0.13. Signing status changes often; check which version you are getting.</p></div>
+        <h4>You need</h4>
+        <ul>
+          <li>A Windows, macOS or Linux computer and a cable.</li>
+          <li><a href="https://github.com/khcrysalis/PlumeImpactor/releases/latest" rel="noopener">PlumeImpactor</a>, the latest release from its official GitHub page, and iTunes if you use Windows.</li>
+          <li>The official <code>Dopamine.ipa</code> on the computer.</li>
+          <li>Your Apple Account. PlumeImpactor uses it to sign the app. Only enter it into the official PlumeImpactor build; some people use a separate Apple Account for sideloading.</li>
+        </ul>
+        <ol class="walk">
+          <li><strong>Connect and trust.</strong> Plug the device into the computer, and make sure the computer is trusted and allowed to view its contents.</li>
+          <li><strong>Sign in to PlumeImpactor.</strong> Open it, go to <em>Settings › Sign In</em>, enter your Apple Account and password, then close the Settings and Sign In windows.</li>
+          <li><strong>Install.</strong> Drag and drop the Dopamine <code>.ipa</code> into PlumeImpactor and click <em>Install</em>. After this, the computer is no longer needed.</li>
+          <li><strong>Trust the app.</strong> On the device go to <em>Settings › General › Device Management</em> (or <em>VPN &amp; Device Management</em> / <em>Profiles and Device Management</em>) › your Apple Account › <em>Trust</em>.</li>
+          <li><strong>Turn on Developer Mode (iOS 16 or later).</strong> If you did not use jailbreaks.app: <em>Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Developer Mode</em>, switch it on and follow the on-screen instructions (the device restarts).</li>
+        </ol>
+        <div class="phones">
+          <figure><img src="../assets/img/sl-trust.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration: Settings, Device Management, showing the Developer App entry for your Apple Account and a Trust button."><figcaption>Step 4 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+          <figure><img src="../assets/img/sl-devmode.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration: Settings, Privacy and Security, with the Developer Mode switch turned on and highlighted."><figcaption>Step 5 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+        </div>
+        <div class="callout callout-warn"><span class="callout-title">Every 7 days</span><p>Apps signed with a regular Apple Account expire after 7 days (365 days with a paid Apple Developer account). After that Dopamine will not open, so you cannot re-jailbreak after a restart until you re-sign it. See <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/sideloading-apps/" rel="noopener">ios.cfw.guide: Sideloading Apps</a>. Already-installed tweaks keep their files; they just are not active while the device is not jailbroken.</p></div>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/installing-dopamine-trollstore/" rel="noopener">Installing Dopamine (TrollStore)</a> and <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/installing-dopamine/" rel="noopener">Installing Dopamine</a> (page sources last changed 7 Aug 2026); <a href="https://github.com/opa334/TrollStore" rel="noopener">TrollStore README</a>; <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/" rel="noopener">ellekit.space/dopamine</a>.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-8">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-10">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
