+<!-- ======================================================================= 10 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-10" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-10-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Installation</p><h2 id="ch-10-h">Running the jailbreak</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <ol class="walk">
+      <li><strong>Reboot the device.</strong> Not required, but recommended by the official guide.</li>
+      <li><strong>Open Dopamine</strong> from the Home Screen immediately afterwards.</li>
+      <li><strong>Tap <em>Jailbreak</em>.</strong> Do not touch the device while it works.
+        <ul>
+          <li>On some 2 GB RAM devices on 15.8.7 – 15.8.8 or 16.7 and later, Dopamine first asks for a respring (<em>Respring Required</em> › <em>Apply Workaround</em>). After the respring, open Dopamine and tap <em>Jailbreak</em> again. On A8 devices this may need several tries.</li>
+          <li>On A12/A13 devices on 16.6 or later the screen briefly turns off and on. That is expected.</li>
+        </ul></li>
+      <li><strong>Choose a package manager</strong> (first run). Dopamine asks you to <em>Select Package Manager(s)</em>: “If you are unsure which one to select, select Sileo”. You can choose both.</li>
+      <li><strong>Wait for the userspace reboot.</strong> The screen goes dark and the Lock Screen returns. Dopamine then shows <em>Jailbroken</em>, and Sileo and/or Zebra are on your Home Screen.</li>
+    </ol>
+    <div class="phones">
+      <figure><img src="../assets/img/dp-main.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration of Dopamine's main screen with the Jailbreak button highlighted."><figcaption>Step 3 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+      <figure><img src="../assets/img/dp-pm.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration of the Select Package Manager(s) screen: the hint “If you are unsure which one to select, select Sileo”, Sileo selected, Zebra not selected, and a Continue button."><figcaption>Step 4 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+      <figure><img src="../assets/img/dp-done.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration of Dopamine's progress log: Exploiting Kernel, Bypassing PAC and PPL, Initializing Environment, Initializing Protection, Rebooting Userspace, ending with Jailbroken."><figcaption>Step 5 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+    </div>
+    <div class="callout callout-tip"><span class="callout-title">If it fails</span><p>“If the app or your device crashes/restarts unexpectedly and the jailbreak isn't installed, simply try rebooting and running the exploit again until it does work.” (ios.cfw.guide). Exploits are not 100% reliable.</p></div>
+
+    <h3>First-time setup: ElleKit and PreferenceLoader</h3>
+    <p>The official guide then updates and installs two essentials in Sileo (<a href="#ch-11">Chapter 11</a> explains the app):</p>
+    <ol class="walk">
+      <li><strong>ElleKit.</strong> <em>Sources</em> tab › <em>ElleKit</em> repository › <em>All Categories</em> › <em>ElleKit</em> › <em>Get</em>.</li>
+      <li><strong>PreferenceLoader.</strong> <em>Search</em> tab › search <code>PreferenceLoader</code> › <em>Get</em>. It lets tweaks add their settings to the Settings app.</li>
+      <li><strong>Confirm.</strong> Tap the <em>Queued</em> bar at the bottom, then <em>Confirm</em>.</li>
+      <li><strong>Tap <em>Reboot Device</em></strong> when it finishes. Despite the name this is not a full reboot: you stay jailbroken.</li>
+    </ol>
+    <div class="phones">
+      <figure><img src="../assets/img/si-sources.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration: Sileo's Sources tab with the ElleKit repository highlighted."><figcaption>Step 1 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+      <figure><img src="../assets/img/si-get.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration: Sileo's ElleKit package page with the Get button, and a Queued bar at the bottom showing 2 items."><figcaption>Steps 1–3 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+      <figure><img src="../assets/img/si-confirm.svg" width="240" height="480" alt="Illustration: Sileo's queue listing ElleKit and PreferenceLoader with a Confirm button, then a Reboot Device button and the note Stays jailbroken afterwards."><figcaption>Steps 3–4 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
+    </div>
+    <p>On 15.0 – 16.6.1, 16.7 RC and 17.0, if you sideloaded Dopamine, the official guide then recommends installing TrollStore through Sileo's <em>TrollStore Helper</em> and reinstalling Dopamine with it, so you never have to re-sign. Follow “Next Steps” on <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/installing-dopamine/" rel="noopener">Installing Dopamine</a>.</p>
+
+    <h3>How to tell it worked</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Dopamine shows <em>Jailbroken</em>.</li>
+      <li>Sileo (or Zebra) opens and refreshes its sources without errors.</li>
+      <li>ElleKit and PreferenceLoader appear under Sileo's installed packages.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <h3>What happens after a reboot</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>After a <strong>full restart</strong> the device starts as normal iOS: no tweaks run. Your jailbreak files and installed packages stay on the device.</li>
+      <li>To jailbreak again: open Dopamine, tap <em>Jailbreak</em>. On the sideload route this only works while the app's 7-day signature is valid.</li>
+      <li>A <strong>respring</strong> (<em>Restart SpringBoard</em>) or <strong>userspace reboot</strong> (<em>Reboot Userspace</em>, or Sileo's <em>Reboot Device</em>) keeps you jailbroken.</li>
+      <li>When Dopamine offers an update, it shows <em>Update Available</em> inside the app.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: ios.cfw.guide <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/installing-dopamine/" rel="noopener">Installing Dopamine</a> (“Running Dopamine”, “Installing necessary software”, “Next Steps”); Dopamine 3.0.13 app strings.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-9">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-11">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
