+<!-- ======================================================================= 11 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-11" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-11-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Package managers</p><h2 id="ch-11-h">Installing and using Sileo or Zebra</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p>A <strong>package manager</strong> is the jailbreak's App Store: it installs, updates and removes tweaks, themes and tools. ios.cfw.guide: they “can be considered similar to the iOS App Store, where you can install both free and paid software.” Dopamine offers two:</p>
+    <div class="compare">
+      <div class="card"><h3>Sileo</h3><p>Dopamine's suggestion if you are unsure, and the one the official setup steps use. Credited on the Dopamine website to Amy While.</p></div>
+      <div class="card"><h3>Zebra</h3><p>An alternative package manager. Credited on the Dopamine website to Adam Demasi. It works with the same sources and packages.</p></div>
+    </div>
+    <p>Chose only one at first? Install the other later with <em>Dopamine › Settings › Reinstall Package Managers</em>. Use one at a time for changes, so two apps do not edit the same package database simultaneously.</p>
+    <h3>Everyday tasks</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li><strong>Add a source:</strong> <em>Sources</em> tab › <em>+</em>, enter the URL exactly (with the trailing slash), let it refresh. Many sites have an “Add to Sileo” or “Add to Zebra” button that fills it in for you.</li>
+      <li><strong>Find a package:</strong> <em>Search</em> tab, or browse a source's categories.</li>
+      <li><strong>Install:</strong> open the package, read its description, compatibility and dependencies, tap <em>Get</em>, then the <em>Queued</em> bar › <em>Confirm</em>.</li>
+      <li><strong>Update:</strong> pull down to refresh sources, then review the available updates. Read changelogs; update a few things at a time.</li>
+      <li><strong>Remove:</strong> find the package among your installed packages, open it and choose <em>Remove</em>, then confirm. Respring if asked.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <h3>Command line (optional)</h3>
+    <p>With a terminal app or SSH, the same database is managed by APT. For example, after adding a source file:</p>
+    <div class="cmd"><pre><code id="cmd-apt-update">sudo apt update</code></pre><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal" data-copy-from="cmd-apt-update">Copy</button></div>
+    <p class="small muted">Commands are shown for you to copy and run yourself; nothing runs from this page.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-10">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-12">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
+
+<!-- ======================================================================= 12 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-12" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-12-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Concepts</p><h2 id="ch-12-h">Understanding repositories and packages</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p>A <strong>repository</strong> (repo, or source) is a website that lists packages. ios.cfw.guide: repos “are essentially databases that contain lots of tweaks for you to install.” A <strong>package</strong> is a <code>.deb</code> file containing a tweak, theme, app or tool, plus a description of what it needs.</p>
+    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Parts of a package listing (scrollable)"><table>
+      <caption>Parts of a package listing</caption>
+      <tbody>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Package ID</th><td>A unique name, e.g. <code>com.hakmicapitalgroup.hcgnexus</code>.</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Version</th><td><code>~beta</code> in a version marks a pre-release.</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Architecture</th><td><code>iphoneos-arm64</code> = rootless (what Dopamine uses). <code>iphoneos-arm</code> = rootful.</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Depends</th><td>Other packages it needs, often <code>preferenceloader</code> and an injector (<code>mobilesubstrate</code> or <code>ellekit</code>), and sometimes a minimum <code>firmware</code> (iOS) version.</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Depiction</th><td>The package's information page: features, compatibility, known issues, changelog.</td></tr>
+      </tbody>
+    </table></div>
+    <h3>Staying safe with sources</h3>
+    <div class="callout callout-danger"><span class="callout-title">Malicious repositories</span>
+      <ul>
+        <li>A package installs with the highest privileges on the device. Add only sources you have a reason to trust, and remove ones you no longer use.</li>
+        <li>Avoid “cracked” or pirated tweak repos. They are a well-known route for malware, and they take income from developers.</li>
+        <li>Never turn off APT signature checking to make a source work.</li>
+        <li>Be wary of any source or tweak that asks for your Apple Account, banking or other passwords.</li>
+      </ul></div>
+    <h3>Avoiding incompatible tweaks</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Read the depiction: is it built for rootless (<code>iphoneos-arm64</code>) and does it list your iOS version?</li>
+      <li>Install one tweak at a time and use your device for a bit before adding the next. When something breaks, you know which one did it.</li>
+      <li>Two tweaks that change the same part of iOS (for example two Lock Screen tweaks) often conflict.</li>
+      <li>“Builds and installs” is not the same as “tested on a device like mine”. Prefer packages whose depiction lists tested devices.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <h3>Example: adding HCG Repo</h3>
+    <p>HCG Repo is one example of a source. Adding it is optional and not needed for Dopamine.</p>
+    <div class="cmd"><pre><code id="cmd-hcg-repo">https://repo.hakmicapitalgroup.com/repo/</code></pre><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal" data-copy-from="cmd-hcg-repo">Copy URL</button></div>
+    <p>Or, from a terminal, as a file under <code>/var/jb/etc/apt/sources.list.d/</code> followed by <code>sudo apt update</code>:</p>
+    <div class="cmd"><pre><code id="cmd-hcg-deb">deb https://repo.hakmicapitalgroup.com/repo/ ./</code></pre><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal" data-copy-from="cmd-hcg-deb">Copy</button></div>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-11">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-13">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
+
+<!-- ======================================================================= 13 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-13" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-13-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div><p class="eyebrow">When things go wrong</p><h2 id="ch-13-h">Safe Mode, troubleshooting and recovery</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <h3>Know your restarts</h3>
+    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Kinds of restart and whether you stay jailbroken (scrollable)"><table>
+      <caption>Kinds of restart and whether you stay jailbroken</caption>
+      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Action</th><th scope="col">What restarts</th><th scope="col">Still jailbroken?</th></tr></thead>
+      <tbody>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Respring</th><td>Only SpringBoard (Home Screen and system interface)</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Userspace reboot</th><td>Everything above the kernel</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
+        <tr><th scope="row">Full reboot / force restart</th><td>The whole device</td><td>No: stock iOS until you run Dopamine</td></tr>
+      </tbody>
+    </table></div>
+    <h3>Safe Mode</h3>
+    <p>In <strong>Safe Mode</strong> the device is jailbroken but no tweaks are loaded, so you can still open Sileo or Zebra and remove the package causing trouble. Dopamine has two ways into it:</p>
+    <ul>
+      <li><strong>You choose it:</strong> <em>Dopamine › Settings › Tweak Injection</em> off, then accept the userspace reboot.</li>
+      <li><strong>Dopamine chooses it:</strong> if iOS hits a userspace panic, Dopamine performs a userspace reboot instead of a full panic, saves a “userspace-panic” log, and turns tweak injection off. If your tweaks suddenly stopped working after a crash, look at <em>Tweak Injection</em>.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>When SpringBoard itself keeps crashing, the system can also come up in a Safe Mode screen with tweaks unloaded. Do not just tap to exit: first remove or disable the tweak you installed or changed last, or SpringBoard may load it again.</p>
+    <div class="callout callout-tip"><span class="callout-title">The universal escape</span><p>Because Dopamine is semi-untethered, a <strong>force restart</strong> always brings you back to normal iOS with no tweaks running. iPhone 8 or later: press and release volume up, press and release volume down, then hold the side button until the Apple logo appears. iPhone 7: hold volume down and the side button. iPhone 6s and SE (1st generation): hold the Home and side (or top) buttons. For iPads, see Apple's “Force restart iPad”.</p></div>
+
+    <h3 id="trouble-h">Troubleshooting</h3>
+    <div class="tools-row"><button type="button" class="linklike" data-details-all="open" aria-controls="trouble-list">Expand all</button><button type="button" class="linklike" data-details-all="close" aria-controls="trouble-list">Collapse all</button></div>
+    <div class="faq" id="trouble-list">
+      <details><summary>Dopamine crashes, or the device restarts during the jailbreak</summary>
+        <p>Normal for exploits now and then. Reboot, open Dopamine immediately, and tap <em>Jailbreak</em> again. Repeat if needed (ios.cfw.guide).</p></details>
+      <details><summary>Dopamine says “Respring Required” before it will jailbreak</summary>
+        <p>Some 2 GB RAM devices need a workaround first. Tap <em>Apply Workaround</em>; after the respring, open Dopamine and tap <em>Jailbreak</em>. On A8 devices it may need several attempts.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>Respring loop after installing or changing a tweak</summary>
+        <ol>
+          <li>Force restart (see above). You boot into stock iOS.</li>
+          <li>Open Dopamine › <em>Settings</em> › turn <em>Tweak Injection</em> off, then jailbreak.</li>
+          <li>Open Sileo or Zebra and remove the tweak you installed or changed last.</li>
+          <li>Turn <em>Tweak Injection</em> back on and accept the userspace reboot.</li>
+        </ol>
+        <p>ios.cfw.guide: “the most likely culprit is your most recently installed/updated tweak”.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>All my tweaks stopped working after a crash</summary>
+        <p>Dopamine turns tweak injection off after it catches a userspace panic. Check <em>Dopamine › Settings › Tweak Injection</em>. Before switching it back on, remove whatever caused the crash.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>The Dopamine app will not open (sideload route)</summary>
+        <p>Its 7-day signature has probably expired. Re-sign it with PlumeImpactor (<a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/sideloading-apps/#resigning-apps" rel="noopener">ios.cfw.guide: Resigning Apps</a>), then jailbreak. On 15.0 – 16.6.1, 16.7 RC and 17.0, consider moving to the TrollStore route.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>TrollStore or apps installed with it will not open</summary>
+        <p>When iOS reloads its icon cache, TrollStore apps revert to a non-launchable state. Open your persistence helper app (often Tips) and tap <em>Refresh App Registrations</em>.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>Sileo, Zebra or other jailbreak app icons are missing</summary>
+        <p>Use <em>Dopamine › Settings › Refresh Jailbreak Apps</em>. From a terminal you can also rebuild the icon cache:</p>
+        <div class="cmd"><pre><code id="cmd-uicache">uicache -a</code></pre><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal" data-copy-from="cmd-uicache">Copy</button></div></details>
+      <details><summary>Dopamine reports duplicate apps and cannot continue</summary>
+        <p>An app that Dopamine ships (for example a package manager) is also installed separately, or registered under a different path. Remove the separately installed copy, then jailbreak again.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>The touchscreen stopped responding after jailbreaking</summary>
+        <p>ios.cfw.guide: on devices with a replacement screen, “especially if the screen is of low quality”, touch may not work after the userspace reboot. This is not a Dopamine bug. Force restart to return to stock iOS.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>Sileo cannot refresh a source, or a package is “not found”</summary>
+        <p>Check the URL exactly, including the trailing slash, and your connection. Packages are hidden when they do not match your layout (rootless) or your iOS version.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>A banking or other app refuses to run</summary>
+        <p>Expected on a jailbroken device. Use another device for it, or remove the jailbreak (Chapter 14). See Chapter 4 for why HCG does not cover bypasses.</p></details>
+      <details><summary>Apple logo over and over, even after a force restart (bootloop)</summary>
+        <p>Rare with a rootless, semi-untethered jailbreak, but possible. ios.cfw.guide: a bootloop “can be diagnosed by looking for a constant re-occuring Apple logo, even after you've forcefully rebooted”, and escaping it needs a restore in DFU mode. A restore <strong>erases the device and installs current iOS</strong>, ending the jailbreak; afterwards restore your backup. Ask for help first (r/jailbreak Discord, linked from ios.cfw.guide) and keep any crash logs.</p></details>
+    </div>
+    <h3>Recovery Mode and DFU</h3>
+    <p><strong>Recovery Mode</strong> lets a computer reinstall iOS when the installed system cannot start. <strong>DFU mode</strong> is a deeper last resort that does not load iOS at all. Both are used by Finder or iTunes for restores, and both normally end with a fresh install of the newest signed iOS. Use them only when a force restart does not get you back.</p>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/troubleshooting/" rel="noopener">ios.cfw.guide: Troubleshooting</a>, <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/faq/" rel="noopener">FAQ</a>; Dopamine 3.0.13 source (<code>DOEnvironmentManager.m</code>, <code>jbdomain_watchdog.c</code>, app strings); <a href="https://github.com/opa334/TrollStore" rel="noopener">TrollStore README</a>.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-12">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-14">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
