+<!-- ======================================================================= 14 -->
+<section class="chapter" id="ch-14" data-chapter aria-labelledby="ch-14-h">
+  <div class="chapter-head"><span class="chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div><p class="eyebrow">The way back</p><h2 id="ch-14-h">Removing a jailbreak</h2></div></div>
+  <div class="chapter-body">
+    <p>“Uninstalling a jailbreak isn't as simple as deleting the app” (ios.cfw.guide). Dopamine removes itself from inside its own app:</p>
+    <ol class="walk">
+      <li><strong>Reboot into a non-jailbroken state.</strong> A normal restart does this.</li>
+      <li><strong>Open Dopamine</strong> and tap <em>Settings</em>.</li>
+      <li><strong>Choose <em>Remove Jailbreak</em>.</strong>
+        <ul>
+          <li>Not installed with TrollStore: leave Settings and tap the <em>Remove Jailbreak</em> button.</li>
+          <li>Installed with TrollStore: tap <em>Continue</em>. This may take a while; if it fails, start again from step 1.</li>
+        </ul></li>
+      <li><strong>Reboot.</strong> Dopamine confirms “Successfully removed jailbreak. Rebooting the device is recommended.”</li>
+    </ol>
+    <div class="callout callout-warn"><span class="callout-title">What it removes, and what it keeps</span><p>Dopamine: removing the jailbreak “will delete all jailbreak-related files, but all regular apps, files and data will be kept … You can't undo this action.” Every tweak, its settings and your sources are gone; re-jailbreaking starts from scratch.</p></div>
+    <h3>Finish cleaning up</h3>
+    <ul>
+      <li>Delete the Dopamine app. Apps installed with TrollStore can only be removed from TrollStore itself (TrollStore README).</li>
+      <li>If you installed an update-blocking profile, remove it under <em>Settings › General › VPN &amp; Device Management</em>. iOS can then update, which normally ends jailbreak support for this device.</li>
+      <li>Turn automatic updates back on, and install the latest iOS to get Apple's security fixes.</li>
+      <li>Before a repair or warranty visit, the most thorough option is to erase and restore the device with a computer, then restore your backup.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p class="small muted">Moving to rootless palera1n? ios.cfw.guide says it is intercompatible with Dopamine, so removal is not required for that. Rootful palera1n is not intercompatible.</p>
+    <p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/removing-dopamine/" rel="noopener">ios.cfw.guide: Removing Dopamine</a> (page source last changed 23 Aug 2026); Dopamine 3.0.13 app strings; <a href="https://github.com/opa334/TrollStore" rel="noopener">TrollStore README</a>; <a href="https://ios.cfw.guide/blocking-updates/" rel="noopener">Blocking Updates</a>.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="chapter-foot"><button type="button" class="btn btn-metal mark-complete" aria-pressed="false">Mark chapter complete</button><p class="chapter-nav"><a href="#ch-13">← Previous</a><a href="#ch-15">Next →</a></p></div>
+</section>
