+<section class="extra chapter" id="glossary-section" aria-labelledby="glossary-h">
+  <h2 id="glossary-h">Glossary</h2>
+  <div class="field glossary-search">
+    <label for="glossary-q">Search the glossary</label>
+    <input class="input" id="glossary-q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. respring" aria-describedby="glossary-count" aria-controls="glossary">
+    <p class="help" id="glossary-count" aria-live="polite">36 terms</p>
+  </div>
+  <dl class="glossary" id="glossary">
+    <div><dt>APT</dt><dd>The package system behind Sileo and Zebra. It downloads packages from repositories and resolves their dependencies.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Bootloop</dt><dd>The device keeps showing the Apple logo and never finishes starting, even after a force restart. Usually needs a restore.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Bootstrap</dt><dd>The base set of command-line tools and libraries a jailbreak installs. Dopamine uses Procursus.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Build number</dt><dd>Apple's exact identifier for an iOS release, e.g. 20H18 for 16.7 RC. Shown in Settings › General › About.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Chip (SoC)</dt><dd>The processor, such as A13 or M1. Jailbreak support depends on it. arm64 chips are A8–A11; arm64e chips are A12 and later.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Code signing</dt><dd>Apple's system for allowing only approved code to run. Sideloaded apps are signed with your own Apple Account for 7 days.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>.deb</dt><dd>A package file: the software plus a description of its version, architecture and dependencies.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Depiction</dt><dd>A package's information page in a package manager or on a repository website.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Developer Mode</dt><dd>An iOS 16+ setting that must be on to run apps you sideloaded yourself.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>DFU mode</dt><dd>Device Firmware Upgrade: a last-resort mode for restoring a device without loading iOS.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>ElleKit</dt><dd>The tweak injection library Dopamine uses, by évelyne. It loads tweaks into apps and system processes.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Exploit</dt><dd>Code that takes advantage of a security flaw. Jailbreaks chain several to gain control of the kernel.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>IPA / TIPA</dt><dd>An iOS app package. Dopamine is distributed as an .ipa; TrollStore also opens .tipa files.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Jailbreak</dt><dd>Using exploits to lift iOS restrictions on your own device so you can run unapproved software and modify the system.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Jetsam</dt><dd>The iOS feature that ends processes using too much memory. Dopamine's Jetsam Multiplier raises the limit; leave it alone unless advised.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Kernel</dt><dd>The core of the operating system that controls memory, hardware and permissions.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Package manager</dt><dd>An app such as Sileo or Zebra that installs, updates and removes jailbreak packages.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>PAC, PPL, SPTM</dt><dd>Apple hardware and kernel protections (Pointer Authentication Codes, Page Protection Layer, Secure Page Table Monitor) that a jailbreak must bypass on newer chips.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Persistence Helper</dt><dd>A system app (often Tips) that TrollStore modifies so it can re-register TrollStore apps after iOS reloads its icon cache.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>PreferenceLoader</dt><dd>A package that lets tweaks add their own pages to the Settings app.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Recovery Mode</dt><dd>A built-in mode in which a computer can reinstall iOS when the device cannot start normally.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Repository (repo, source)</dt><dd>A website that lists packages for package managers.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Respring</dt><dd>Restarting SpringBoard (the Home Screen and system interface). You stay jailbroken.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Rootful</dt><dd>An older jailbreak layout that writes into the system volume. Packages use <code>iphoneos-arm</code>.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Rootless</dt><dd>The layout Dopamine uses: all jailbreak files live under <code>/var/jb</code> and the system volume is left alone. Packages use <code>iphoneos-arm64</code>.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Roothide</dt><dd>A third layout with a randomised jailbreak root. Not used by Dopamine; packages use <code>iphoneos-arm64e</code>.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Safe Mode</dt><dd>A jailbroken state with tweaks turned off, used to remove a problem tweak.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Semi-untethered</dt><dd>A jailbreak that must be re-applied with an app on the device after every full reboot. Dopamine is one.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Sideloading</dt><dd>Installing an app from outside the App Store by signing it with your own Apple Account, using a computer tool such as PlumeImpactor.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Sileo</dt><dd>A package manager for jailbroken devices, and Dopamine's default suggestion.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>SpringBoard</dt><dd>The iOS process that draws the Home Screen, Lock Screen and system interface.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>TrollStore</dt><dd>An app that permanently installs other apps through a code-signing bug. Works only on 14.0 beta 2 – 16.6.1, 16.7 RC and 17.0.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Tweak</dt><dd>A small modification that changes how iOS or an app looks or behaves. Usually configured in Settings, not with its own icon.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Tweak injection</dt><dd>Loading tweaks into running apps and processes. Dopamine's Tweak Injection switch turns it on and off.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>Userspace reboot</dt><dd>Restarting everything above the kernel without a full reboot. Dopamine and Sileo use it; you stay jailbroken.</dd></div>
+    <div><dt>/var/jb</dt><dd>The path where a rootless jailbreak keeps its files. It points to a hidden folder in <code>/private/preboot</code>.</dd></div>
+  </dl>
+</section>
